{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And He blessed them</b> — meaning, that the human species not be cut off. <b>And He said</b> etc. — He commanded them to be fruitful and multiply, for even though He blessed them that the human species should endure, they might not for that reason be lax from being fruitful and multiplying. I have seen corrupt views among created beings from among our people: when there are three or four brothers, one or two of them engage in procreation and say, 'This is the perpetuation of the species.' Even regarding a single man — when he has ensured his species, the thought may occur to him not to engage further in being fruitful and multiplying. Therefore HaShem, at the beginning of divine utterance, the commandment of HaShem from the outset, said <b>Be fruitful and multiply</b>, and set no boundary to the commandment, even though He blessed them that the human species not be cut off from the world. And He finished saying <b>and fill the earth</b>. And His saying <b>and subdue it</b> adjacent to 'and fill it' is to say that through the very act of filling the earth, it will be subdued before them — for a desolate place, a person does not rule over it, because by virtue of its desolation it is filled with adversaries to man. It further intends, in His saying <b>and He blessed them</b>, that there be within them the procreative power, and afterward He commanded them concerning the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:57:30.161551940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}